index fa1a2d5..ff7e73d 100644
--- a/CHANGELOG.md
+++ b/CHANGELOG.md
@@ -8,6 +8,14 @@ package, not for somebody reading this repository's commit log.
 
 ## [Unreleased]
 
+### Added
+
+- Tool input is now validated. `ToolRegistry.execute` checks the input a model sends against the tool's declared `inputSchema` (the same schema your providers already receive) before the executor runs, using [`ajv`](https://www.npmjs.com/package/ajv). Input the schema rejects never reaches your executor: the registry returns a tool result naming the failing property and constraint -- never the offending value -- so the model can read the rejection and correct its call within the existing tool-round budget. A static tool's schema is compiled once at `register` time, so a broken schema fails at startup; schemas returned by a function-valued definition source are compiled per distinct schema object. Undeclared extra properties pass through to the executor unchanged, and there is no opt-out.
+
+### Changed
+
+- If your executor hand-validated its input, that check is now redundant: it only ever sees input the declared schema accepts. A tool that relied on seeing malformed input to produce its own error message stops seeing it -- the registry's rejection is the error message, and the failure mode for a malformed call is a returned tool result rather than whatever your executor used to do. Validate less, and declare the schema you actually want enforced.
+
 ## [0.3.0] - 2026-09-17
 
 ### Changed
